    "region_id": "mount-rogers",
    "name": "Mount Rogers & Grayson Highlands (Southwest Virginia)",
    "region_label": "Mount Rogers",
    "description": "Virginia's high country in the far southwest: Mount Rogers (5,729 ft — the state's highest peak) and Whitetop Mountain in the Mount Rogers National Recreation Area (Jefferson National Forest), plus adjoining Grayson Highlands State Park with its open balds and free-roaming wild ponies. The Appalachian Trail and the Virginia Creeper Trail thread the area; Damascus is the classic AT trail town on the west edge. High, rugged terrain — steep elevation profiles are correct.",
    "bbox": [-81.85, 36.55, -81.3, 36.85],
    "bbox_comment": "[west, south, east, north] in decimal degrees (WGS84). Tight around the Mount Rogers high country: Damascus (W), Troutdale/NRA HQ (N), Grayson Highlands and Mount Rogers/Whitetop (core), Mouth of Wilson (SE).",
    "sources": ["OSM", "USGS"],
    "area_ids": ["usfs:mount-rogers-nra", "va:grayson-highlands-sp"],
